worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_orientation_cue_fairness_claude/orientation_cue_fairness_codex_code_round2_close10_review.md:121:The trainer takes only `.registration.lock`; it does not require `.publish.lock`. Full mode holds publication ownership from before its scan through the child run and publication. The frozen lifecycle also waits for the log sink, so wrapper death alone did not release that protection.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_orientation_cue_fairness_claude/orientation_cue_fairness_codex_code_round2_close10_review.md:123:For an orphan with an incomplete `child.pid`, the marker and registration/resolution lock cover delayed registration correctly. The wrapper-loss case in blocker 2 invalidates the broader claim that all startup states are covered.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_orientation_cue_fairness_claude/orientation_cue_fairness_codex_code_round2_close10_review.md:125:A stuck registration-lock holder causes an ordinary trainer startup to fail after approximately 60 seconds. Scans do not queue on that lock, and resolution acquires it non-blockingly. The resolver’s filesystem operations have no separate hard deadline. Also, [tools/exp11_train.py:238](/home/yixunhu/codespace/xRIR_code_wt/tools/exp11_train.py:238) uses `time.time()`; switching to `time.monotonic()` would make the elapsed-time bound robust against backward clock adjustments.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_orientation_cue_fairness_claude/orientation_cue_fairness_codex_code_round2_close10_review.md:127:The arm-root `.registration.lock` is a regular file outside the attempts. It cannot match `scan_arm`’s `attempt_*` directory walk. Finalizer preflight reads `*/launch.pid` and `*/child.pid`, while full evidence is checked inside the selected attempt; neither treats this root lock file as run evidence.
